Thought: The frontend logs show DNS lookup failures for currencyservice and checkoutservice plus a cartservice TCP timeout, while all pods are Running. I’ll test internal service connectivity to currencyservice first, since DNS failure there is the dominant error pattern.
Action: CheckServiceConnectivity
Action Input: {"service_name": "currencyservice", "port": 7000, "namespace": "boutique"}

Thought: Connectivity to currencyservice succeeds from worker-02 and worker-03 but fails from worker-01, indicating a node-local networking/dataplane problem rather than a service-level DNS issue. I’ll verify kube-proxy health on worker-01.
Action: CheckNodeServiceStatus
Action Input: {"node_name": "worker-01", "service_name": "kube-proxy"}

Thought: Evidence is conclusive — kube-proxy on worker-01 is inactive (dead), and the connectivity test shows ClusterIP reachability failing only from worker-01 while succeeding from worker-02/03. This explains the frontend's connection errors (i/o timeout to cartservice ClusterIP, DNS lookups failing when pods on worker-01 can't reach the DNS service VIP). Root cause: kube_proxy_unavailable on node/worker-01.
